KG42.register("source_edge_archive-3da0e6a9e8627fbaa51dada8",{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E001","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","rule_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e015"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004-C003"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-84de1f1af39d310b","target":"COMP-276b46f772c03e0a","source_occurrence_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","target_occurrence_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal","source_unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","target_unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Buyer consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Preparation of internal price signals for the next time slot in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Price-mediated consumption decisions of PV prosumers in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Seller consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g03-E01"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"96227d34da29eb911ede1c5d5dfeaeb58533de26339c51bc5c2eb61b95542c0a","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"The MGO determines the internal buying and selling prices simultaneously and obtains next-slot prices by solving the pricing optimization. Scope: Stackelberg ESM internal buying and selling prices for the next time slot. The MGO increases the internal selling price p_s in the reported shortage cases. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16. Condition: Selling energy is less than buying energy in these reported time slots. The MGO decreases the internal buying price p_b in the reported surplus cases. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 13 and 14. Condition: Selling energy is more than buying energy in these reported time slots. Internal buying and selling prices are decision variables for maximizing the MGO's own profit, subject to λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. Scope: Stackelberg ESM internal-price optimization. Initial internal selling and buying prices may be set to λ^s and λ^b, respectively. Scope: Initialization of internal prices for each time slot. Condition: Initial price setting. Select the internal price pair by comparing MGO profit at the optima of D_1 and D_2, where D_1 applies when E^b \u003c E^s and D_2 applies when E^b ≥ E^s. Scope: Selection of optimal internal prices across the surplus and nonsurplus pricing regions. The internal selling and buying prices remain at λ^s and λ^b, respectively, in these reported time slots. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 7 and 17–19 only. Condition: PV energy is entirely self-consumed and no energy is feasible to trade inside the microgrid.","target_definition":"Internal buying and selling prices coordinate decentralized consumption decisions: prosumers adjust their consumption and choose optimal consumption in response to these prices. Scope: Price-mediated consumption decisions of PV prosumers in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. An increase in p_s may induce sellers to reduce consumption and thereby increase the energy they sell. Scope: Seller consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. Condition: The internal selling price p_s increases. A decrease in p_b may induce buyers to increase consumption and thereby increase the energy they buy. Scope: Buyer consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. Condition: The internal buying price p_b decreases. The MGO solves the internal-price optimization before distributing the resulting internal prices to all prosumers as coordination signals. Scope: Preparation of internal price signals for the next time slot in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Internal buying and selling prices coordinate decentralized consumption decisions: prosumers adjust their consumption and choose optimal consumption in response to these prices. Scope: Price-mediated consumption decisions of PV prosumers in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e015"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"An increase in p_s may induce sellers to reduce consumption and thereby increase the energy they sell. Scope: Seller consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. Condition: The internal selling price p_s increases.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e011"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A decrease in p_b may induce buyers to increase consumption and thereby increase the energy they buy. Scope: Buyer consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. Condition: The internal buying price p_b decreases.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e011"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e006","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p02-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","anchor_text":"g p p mentioned studies, two main differences have been made. The as ﬁrst is the role of participant","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"In this paper, every prosumer has equal privilege which means prosumers are participated in the microgrid operation equipotently. Thus, we select MGO as the leader, which means that the MGO determines the buying and selling prices simultaneously. And the prosumers act as followers to adjust their energy consumption behaviors according to the time-varying prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e011","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model / II.B Profit Model","anchor_text":"The slot, the initial internal prices ps and pb can be set as λs and red λb, respectively. With the ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"With the increase of p_s, it is possible for seller to decrease the consumption and thus the selling energy will increase. Similarly, with the decrease of p_b, it is possible for buyers to increase the consumption and thus the buying energy will increase. Thus, the role of buyer or seller will not be transformed in response to the setting of internal prices. Hence, although (1) is a piecewise function, and p_b is different from p_s, the utility of a buyer or a seller is the continuously differentiable function of the consumption x_n."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e015","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.A Formulation of Stackelberg Game","anchor_text":"LIU et al.: ENERGY SHARING MANAGEMENT FOR MICROGRIDS WITH PV PROSUM by changing their energy consump","equation_id":"(6)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The game is formally defined by its strategic form as L = {(G ∪ {MGO}), {X_n}_{n∈G}, {P_b}, {P_s}, {U_n}_{n∈G}, R} (6) which consists of the following components: 1) The prosumers in set G act as followers and choose their optimal consumption in response to the internal prices set by the MGO, the leader of the game. 2) X_n is the set of strategies of prosumer n, which is constrained by x_n^min ≤ x_n ≤ x_n^max. 3) P_b and P_s are the sets of strategies set by MGO, which are the vectors of the internal prices p_b and p_s, respectively. It should be ensured that the internal prices are constrained by λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b_n. 4) U_n is the utility function of prosumer n, as shown in (1) that captures the prosumer's benefit from consuming energy x_n and sharing energy E_n^g − x_n with other prosumers in the microgrid. 5) R is the profit function of MGO, as shown in (5) that captures the total profit incurred by the sharing energy inside the microgrid and trading with the utility grid."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Buyer consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Preparation of internal price signals for the next time slot in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Price-mediated consumption decisions of PV prosumers in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Seller consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g03-E01"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e015"]},"paper_scope_note":"Stackelberg ESM, deviation billing, and the Cournot baseline are kept separate; buying/selling branches, numerical cases, and the no-deviation/penalty conditions are retained with the declaration."}});
